# tests/budget_guarantees_test.tg — third-audit item 45 (the complete
# @budget system) behavior lane.
#
# The model lives in tg_compiler/types.tg (the BudgetGuarantee record, the
# BudgetDerivations context, budget_classification_of and the derivation-
# aware guarantee/violation rules) and the enforcement pass lives in
# tg_compiler/mir.tg (check_budget_annotations_mir /
# check_budget_annotations_mir_with_frames — the E0235 diagnostics). This
# test drives the self-checking lane rows of budget_guarantee_lane_check:
#   T1 the vocabulary canonicalization (heap_allocations / heap_bytes /
#      stack_bytes / code_size_bytes / time_us / instructions + the
#      unknown-metric passthrough);
#   T2 the strongest classification per resource (heap_allocations
#      static-proof, heap_bytes static-bound, stack_bytes static-proof,
#      code_size_bytes static-bound, instructions static-bound, time_us
#      runtime-measured, unknown runtime-measured) + the closed word set;
#   T3 heap_allocations = 0 with the proven no-alloc summary is static-
#      proof with derived 0; any site downgrades to runtime-measured;
#   T4 heap_bytes is static-bound (derived = sites × the documented
#      per-site cap) outside the zero proof; the zero case is static-proof;
#      the over-limit/within-limit violation rows;
#   T5 stack_bytes is static-proof with the exact LIR frame_bytes and
#      static-bound with the MIR-only derivation; the over-limit row;
#   T6 code_size_bytes is static-bound from the estimate and static-proof
#      with an exact emitted word count;
#   T7 instructions is static-bound with the derivation and runtime-
#      measured without one; time_us is runtime-measured and never yields
#      a static violation row;
#   T8 the time_us bare bound is microseconds, an explicit suffix wins,
#      and the derivation text renders the classification;
#   T9 (fourth-audit P1-7) the four-way heap-size lattice and aggregate
#      rules: a runtime-capacity Vec site is Unbounded/never finite, and
#      an Unbounded/Unknown heap aggregate FAILS the heap_bytes
#      annotation (no finite static proof);
#   T10 (fourth-audit P1-8) the call-graph max-stack analysis with
#      hand-built frames/edges: f (64-byte frame) calling g (256-byte
#      frame) has max_stack 64 + 256 + BUDGET_CALL_OVERHEAD_BYTES; a call
#      cycle (no proven finite recursion bound) and an unknown callee are
#      Unbounded; the stack_bytes rules compare max_stack_bytes (not just
#      the frame) and report both frame_bytes and max_stack_bytes.
#
# Run with the repo root as the working directory:
#   tg test tests/budget_guarantees_test.tg

use std::test::assert

use tg_compiler::types::{budget_guarantee_lane_check}

@test
def test_budget_guarantee_classification_lane() -> Unit
  let rows = budget_guarantee_lane_check()
  assert(rows.len() == 0, "budget guarantee lane mismatches: " + rows.join("; "))
end
